Description: Production retry/budget primitive for LLM and agent calls
 The retry/budget primitive tenacity isn't, with the three things that
 matter for production LLM-shaped work: cost cap, structured per-attempt
 events, and adversarial-loop detection. Wraps any callable with
 max_attempts, max_cost_usd, max_wall_clock_s, retry_on/fatal_on
 exception sets, exponential backoff (clamped to remaining wall-clock),
 and structured AttemptEvent lifecycle hooks. Detects retry-amplification
 via error fingerprinting (closes Instructor #2056 class of bug). Zero
 runtime dependencies; pure Python stdlib at runtime.
